      "item": "thm-parabolic-kl-polynomials-give-the-dual-canonical-transition-matrix",
      "finding": "Step 2.2 says, 'The singular ordinary multiplicity theorem of [F3] has exactly these indices for the sorted-entry stabilizer,' referring to P_{d(C)w₀,d(A)w₀}(1). Its Statement and step 1.1 explicitly make d(A) = w_A⁻¹ minimal LEFT modulo K, whereas thm-singular-category-o-multiplicities-are-parabolic-kl-polynomials accepts minimal RIGHT labels. The tuple identity a(A) = b d(A), with b sorted, gives actual singular weight label w_A = d(A)⁻¹. The desired coefficient is recoverable: apply the supplier to w_C,w_A, then simultaneous inversion and conjugation by w₀ give P_{w_Cw₀,w_Aw₀} = P_{d(C)w₀,d(A)w₀}. This bridge is implicit; the assertion that the supplier has exactly the displayed input indices omits its representative-side hypothesis.",
      "severity": "gap-a-reader-closes"
    }
  ],
